/- ---- D3 SEEDS (program-data parameters E-A, 2026-09-20; record §1/§4). On the
   Lean target the enum map is an ambient reader whose value at the desugar
   entry is EMPTY; the OCaml desugarer reads the registry AS OF THE MOMENT.
   So every desugar-time path into the enum-reading typing/layout functions
   goes through a `reader_seed` def whose seeds are the enums registered SO
   FAR (the sigma-so-far's / desugar state's enum_definitions) and the
   enclosing tag-definition binder — the Lean value then equals the OCaml
   registry's content at that moment (register_tag_definition inserts into
   tag_definitions right after register_enum; nothing else registers). The
   seed defs take one value per declared reader in the sorted order (en,
   tds), then the wrapped function's own arguments; on OCaml the seeds are
   DEAD (the [USER 2026-09-04] exception). Their vals fix the seeds' types
   (a seed used only by injection would otherwise generalise — record W11);
   the two seeds have DIFFERENT types, so a positional slip (audit N1) is a
   type error, not a silent value change. -/

