/- the desugarer's two direct typing calls (typeof(e), sizeof e).
   CLOSURE HAZARD (pre-merge audit E1, 2026-09-20 — record §10): a reader_seed
   re-seeds only what is constructed INSIDE its extent. The block-typing
   callback `GenTyping.annotate_block ret_ty` is itself reader-lifted, so a
   callback built at the CALL SITE (outside the seed) is already applied to
   the caller's binders — the desugar entry's EMPTY enum map — and forwarding
   it into the seed cannot re-seed it (`typeof(({ enum E e = A; unsigned int
   *p = &e; p; }))` crashed on Lean while the oracle ran it). The seed therefore
   takes the DATA the callback is built from (the enclosing return type) and
   constructs the callback in its own body. lem-lean design follow-up (a doc
   sentence at the next lem-lean touch, not this slice): "a reader_seed does
   not re-seed closures constructed outside its extent". -/

